    Compile V4.1's fixed decode shapes into its decode matvecs
    
    Some V4.1 decode matrix-vector products always run with the same sizes: the attention q_a and kv projections, the MoE gate and up projections, the attention output projection and the FFN's hyper-connection merge. They now use kernel variants with those sizes written in as constants, so the compiler can unroll the loops and fold the index math. The results are bit-identical. This extends Ivan Fioravanti's fixed-size kernels to more calls.
    
    DS4_METAL_DISABLE_V41_LITERAL_SHAPES=1 uses the general kernels.

